cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SYNAX (.sx): A Neuro-Symbolic Compiler and Differentially Verified Adaptive SIMD Runtime"
message: "If you use SYNAX (.sx) or its Myelin runtime in academic or computational research, please cite this software using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Aydın"
    given-names: "Ömer Faruk"
    email: "ofaemd@gmail.com"
version: "0.5.0"
date-released: "2026-11-03"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ofaemd-creator/synax"
url: "https://synaxcode.org"
abstract: >-
  SYNAX (.sx) is an open-source neuro-symbolic compiler and adaptive runtime
  system that lowers declarative and structured numerical kernels into
  differentially verified C11, ARM64 NEON, and multicore native code without
  -ffast-math semantic compromises, featuring bitwise IEEE-754 non-finite
  sanitization and O(1) function-pointer hot-swapping.
keywords:
  - neuro-symbolic compiler
  - differential verification
  - IEEE-754
  - SIMD
  - ARM64 NEON
  - adaptive runtime
  - biomedical signal processing
